#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:78
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:124
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:186
msgid "XML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:80
msgid ""
"Copy and paste the complete code into the ``launch/turtlesim_mimic_launch."
"xml`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:82
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"<launch>\n"
"  <node pkg=\"turtlesim\" exec=\"turtlesim_node\" name=\"sim\" "
"namespace=\"turtlesim1\" args=\"--ros-args --log-level info\" />\n"
"  <node pkg=\"turtlesim\" exec=\"turtlesim_node\" name=\"sim\" "
"namespace=\"turtlesim2\" ros_args=\"--log-level warn\" />\n"
"  <node pkg=\"turtlesim\" exec=\"mimic\" name=\"mimic\">\n"
"    <remap from=\"/input/pose\" to=\"/turtlesim1/turtle1/pose\" />\n"
"    <remap from=\"/output/cmd_vel\" to=\"/turtlesim2/turtle1/cmd_vel\" />\n"
"  </node>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:85
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:138
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:193
msgid "YAML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:87
msgid ""
"Copy and paste the complete code into the ``launch/turtlesim_mimic_launch."
"yaml`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:89
msgid ""
"%YAML 1.2\n"
"---\n"
"launch:\n"
"  - node:\n"
"      pkg: \"turtlesim\"\n"
"      exec: \"turtlesim_node\"\n"
"      name: \"sim\"\n"
"      namespace: \"turtlesim1\"\n"
"      args: \"--ros-args --log-level info\"\n"
"\n"
"  - node:\n"
"      pkg: \"turtlesim\"\n"
"      exec: \"turtlesim_node\"\n"
"      name: \"sim\"\n"
"      namespace: \"turtlesim2\"\n"
"      ros_args: \"--log-level warn\"\n"
"\n"
"  - node:\n"
"      pkg: \"turtlesim\"\n"
"      exec: \"mimic\"\n"
"      name: \"mimic\"\n"
"      remap:\n"
"        - from: \"/input/pose\"\n"
"          to: \"/turtlesim1/turtle1/pose\"\n"
"        - from: \"/output/cmd_vel\"\n"
"          to: \"/turtlesim2/turtle1/cmd_vel\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:92
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:152
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:200
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:94
msgid ""
"Copy and paste the complete code into the ``launch/turtlesim_mimic_launch."
"py`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:96
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch_ros.actions import Node\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        Node(\n"
"            package='turtlesim',\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim1',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node',\n"
"            name='sim',\n"
"            arguments=['--ros-args', '--log-level', 'info']\n"
"        ),\n"
"        Node(\n"
"            package='turtlesim',\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim2',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node',\n"
"            name='sim',\n"
"            ros_arguments=['--log-level', 'warn']\n"
"        ),\n"
"        Node(\n"
"            package='turtlesim',\n"
"            executable='mimic',\n"
"            name='mimic',\n"
"            remappings=[\n"
"                ('/input/pose', '/turtlesim1/turtle1/pose'),\n"
"                ('/output/cmd_vel', '/turtlesim2/turtle1/cmd_vel'),\n"
"            ]\n"
"        )\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:101
msgid "2.1 Examine the launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:103
msgid ""
"All of the launch files above are launching a system of three nodes, all "
"from the ``turtlesim`` package. The goal of the system is to launch two "
"turtlesim windows, and have one turtle mimic the movements of the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:106
msgid ""
"When launching the two turtlesim nodes, the primary difference between them "
"is their namespace values. Unique namespaces allow the system to start two "
"nodes without node name or topic name conflicts. Both turtles in this system "
"receive commands over the same topic and publish their pose over the same "
"topic. With unique namespaces, messages meant for different turtles can be "
"distinguished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:111
msgid ""
"The two turtlesim nodes also demonstrate different ways to pass arguments to "
"nodes. The first node uses ``args`` to pass arguments directly to the "
"executable, requiring the ``--ros-args`` flag for ROS-specific arguments. "
"The second node uses ``ros_args`` (``ros_arguments`` in Python), designed "
"specifically for ROS arguments. Use ``args`` when mixing ROS and non-ROS "
"arguments (e.g., ``my_custom_arg --ros-args --log-level info``), or "
"``ros_args`` for cleaner syntax with only ROS arguments like remappings, "
"parameters, or log levels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:116
msgid ""
"The final node is also from the ``turtlesim`` package, but a different "
"executable: ``mimic``. This node has added configuration details in the form "
"of remappings. ``mimic``'s ``/input/pose`` topic is remapped to ``/"
"turtlesim1/turtle1/pose`` and it's ``/output/cmd_vel`` topic to ``/"
"turtlesim2/turtle1/cmd_vel``. This means ``mimic`` will subscribe to ``/"
"turtlesim1/sim``'s pose topic and republish it for ``/turtlesim2/sim``'s "
"velocity command topic to subscribe to. In other words, ``turtlesim2`` will "
"mimic ``turtlesim1``'s movements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:126
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:140
msgid ""
"The first two actions launch the two turtlesim windows with different "
"argument passing approaches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Creating-Launch-Files.rst:128
